AB  - This report argues that a U.S. infrastructure package should prioritize digital infrastructure investments alongside traditional physical projects. It emphasizes that digital infrastructure, including broadband, smart grids, and digitized physical systems, offers superior long-term economic growth, competitiveness, and national security benefits compared to solely focusing on traditional infrastructure. The report advocates for significant funding for digital upgrades to government IT, smart cities, farms, and factories, cautioning that neglecting these areas risks the U.S. falling behind countries like China. It stresses that infrastructure investments should focus on spurring productivity growth and enhancing U.S. competitiveness, rather than solely on short-term job creation.
