AB  - This report provides a biweekly update on the developments in civilian and military artificial intelligence (AI) in Russia. It highlights a government survey revealing challenges in the Russian AI sector despite job satisfaction among specialists. The report also covers advancements in military AI, including the development of vampire drones, unmanned helicopters, and powerline-recharging drones. Furthermore, it discusses Moscow's ongoing experimentation with Smart City surveillance technologies and universities' projects to enhance Russia's competitiveness in education and technology, as well as Russian engagement in UNESCO's ethical AI recommendations.
