AB  - This document presents written evidence from Big Brother Watch to the Joint Committee on Human Rights concerning the right to privacy in the digital revolution, focusing on mass surveillance, policing technologies, and automation in public services. The submission highlights concerns about the lack of transparency and public consultation surrounding the adoption of new technologies by public authorities, particularly regarding facial recognition, predictive policing, and welfare systems. Big Brother Watch recommends amendments to the Data Protection Act 2018, particularly concerning automated decisions, and calls for a ban on micro-targeted online advertising. They argue that the government should set a good example by respecting citizens' privacy and ensuring adequate legal protections in the face of rapid technological advancements.
