AB  - This notice announces a public meeting of the Homeland Security Science and Technology Advisory Committee (HSSTAC) scheduled for November 3-4, 2016, in Washington, D.C. The meeting will feature open sessions for both in-person and webinar participants, covering topics such as commercialization, social media, IoT smart cities, and the Quadrennial Homeland Security Review (QHSR). The committee will also discuss emerging threats to national security, S&amp;T priorities, and the strategic plan for the Science and Technology Directorate. Members of the public are invited to attend and provide comments on the agenda items.
