AB  - This Defense Innovation Board (DIB) report examines the evolving 5G ecosystem and its implications for the Department of Defense (DoD). It highlights the potential benefits of 5G, including increased data speed, volume, and reduced latency, enabling advancements in autonomous vehicles, smart cities, and military applications. The report emphasizes the importance of first-mover advantage in wireless technology generations, noting that the U.S. risks falling behind China in the global 5G landscape due to spectrum allocation strategies. It assesses the competitive field and offers recommendations for DoD to effectively leverage 5G while mitigating security and supply chain risks.
