AB  - This study investigates the potential applications and technologies for compact, high-accuracy clocks on small satellites, offering GNSS-independent timing solutions with improved accuracy and stability. It explores opportunities for enhancing precision timing in various sectors, including smart cities, electronic warfare, resilient timing distribution, and solar system navigation. The project aims to develop technologies that leverage a highly accurate and stable timing solution, independent of GNSS, and interlinks with the development of a compact optical clock for small satellites. The study will deliver market analysis and simulation-based analysis to assess the feasibility and performance of the space-based clock.
