AB  - This document is a call to Members of the European Parliament to reject amendments to the LIBE Committee report on Artificial Intelligence in criminal law. The signatories, a coalition of organizations and individuals, argue that adopting the proposed amendments would undermine fundamental rights such as the right to a fair trial, privacy, non-discrimination, and the presumption of innocence. They specifically oppose amendments related to predictive policing, facial recognition, and biometric mass surveillance, asserting these technologies pose a serious threat to democratic principles and could disproportionately harm marginalized groups. The coalition urges the EP to uphold the original report's balanced stance on AI in law enforcement, emphasizing the need for careful scrutiny and democratic oversight.
