AB  - A coalition of organizations urges Members of the European Parliament (MEPs) Brando Benifei and Dragoş Tudorache to uphold fundamental rights protections during the trilogue negotiations on the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Act. The letter emphasizes the importance of regulating AI use in law enforcement, migration, and national security, resisting pressure to weaken essential safeguards. It highlights the Parliament's position on banning biometric mass surveillance, emotion recognition, and predictive policing, warning against loopholes that could compromise transparency and accountability, and calling for the preservation of fundamental rights impact assessments (FRIAs). The signatories advocate for an AI Act that prioritizes the rights of EU citizens.
