AB  - This document outlines the Federation of Indian Chambers of Commerce &amp; Industry's (FICCI) recommendations regarding the draft "Geospatial Information Regulation Bill, 2016" in India. FICCI acknowledges the importance of the bill in ensuring national security and integrity but suggests modifications to promote industry growth, avoid hindering citizen benefits, and prevent adverse effects on government initiatives like Smart Cities and Digital India. Key recommendations include streamlining the data acquisition process through a registration portal, clarifying regulations on existing data, ensuring smooth data dissemination, defining sensitive vs. non-sensitive information, providing accurate national boundary data, and refining the security vetting process and penalties.
