AB  - This document explores smart public health emergency management in the context of sustainable smart cities. It focuses on ICT implementations, particularly IoT, AI, and data-driven frameworks, for timely responses to epidemics and pandemics. The study examines existing public health frameworks and provides case studies, including Seoul's response to the COVID-19 pandemic. The work proposes a smart public health framework that defines a pandemic lifecycle and outlines the application of mass surveillance tools during outbreaks. It links smart city initiatives to the UN's Sustainable Development Goals, emphasizing resilience and the use of technology for predicting disease spread, coordinating lockdowns, and providing remote assistance.
