AB  - This report examines the competition between the United States and China in the emerging technology of Light Detection and Ranging (LiDAR). It discusses LiDAR technology, its development, and various applications, including automotive, agriculture, military and smart cities. The report highlights how Chinese firms are advancing in the LiDAR market through industrial policies, acquisitions, and partnerships, sometimes using questionable practices to obtain intellectual property. It also explores potential national security implications due to the use of PRC LiDAR systems in the U.S. and discusses issues for Congress to consider in ensuring fair competition and protecting U.S. interests.
