AB  - This paper examines the potential threat of fully autonomous weapons to the human rights of marginalized communities, particularly people of color. It argues that AI technologies, including those used in autonomous weapons, are not racially neutral and can perpetuate and amplify existing biases. The paper highlights examples of racism in AI, such as under-representation in STEM, biased facial recognition systems, and discriminatory predictive policing. It calls for a legally binding instrument to prohibit fully autonomous weapons and preserve meaningful human control over the use of force.
