AB  - The ACLU submits comments regarding the use of facial recognition technology (FRT), fingerprint, iris, DNA technologies, and predictive policing algorithms by law enforcement agencies. It raises civil rights and civil liberties concerns, including unjustified arrests, exacerbating racism in policing, and violating privacy rights. The ACLU advocates for a federal moratorium on FRT use by law and immigration enforcement, highlighting its unreliability, bias, and potential for mass surveillance. The comments emphasize the need for transparency and robust protections, and call for a ban on technologies with no safe use.
