AB  - This report summarizes the activities of the Vivekananda International Foundation (VIF) from March to early April 2020. It includes a daily scan of international COVID-19 developments, commentaries on topics like the role of the Chinese government in the coronavirus crisis, Myanmar's economy, and the Indo-Pacific meeting on COVID-19. Articles cover cyber warfare, the US-Taliban deal, disaster resilience in Indian smart cities, and China's use of 4IR technologies during the pandemic. The report also features national security briefs, news digests, scholar outreach, conference participation, and social media engagement, along with website analytics and popular videos.
