AB  - This document chronicles Manchester's evolution as a "modern internet city" over four decades, tracing its journey from early digital innovation and activism to its current status as a "smart city." It highlights key developments such as the Poptel project, the Manchester Host Computer Communications &amp; Information Network, the establishment of community ICT access centers, and the city's role in the "Information City" and "Smart City" initiatives. The text also touches upon the influence of academic and military research, activist networking, the digital divide, and the emergence of user-generated content. It emphasizes Manchester's pioneering efforts in digital infrastructure, community engagement, and open innovation, including its participation in European smart city networks and the "Living Lab" concept.
