AB  - The National Timing Centre (NTC) programme, led by the National Physical Laboratory (NPL), aims to establish a trusted and assured time and frequency distribution system across the UK. Recognizing the vulnerabilities of Global Navigation Satellite Systems (GNSS) and the increasing reliance on precise timing data for critical infrastructure, digital services, and emerging technologies like autonomous vehicles and smart cities, the NTC programme seeks to provide a resilient alternative. It will leverage multiple time distribution technologies, including fiber, satellites, and terrestrial broadcasts, alongside GNSS. The program also includes developing a new atomic clock network, fostering innovation through partnerships with Innovate UK, and addressing skills shortages in the field. This initiative is crucial for national security, economic stability, and technological advancement.
