AB  - This document details the National Leadership Grants awarded in FY 2017, Cycle Two, for various library initiatives across the United States. The grants support projects focused on developing citizen science toolkits, advancing digital archiving practices, exploring blockchain technology for library services, fostering computational literacy, assessing big data curation capacity, supporting community data reusers, adapting arts programming for rural libraries, enhancing collections related to racial representation, improving repository software performance, designing inclusive library information systems, strengthening information literacy programs, supporting school libraries in mental health literacy, establishing standards for 3D data preservation, developing childcare provider training programs, managing digital government records, creating tools for linked open data from archives, exploring libraries' roles in smart city initiatives, archiving the web and social media ethically, automating data extraction from archival slides, developing open educational resources for scholarly communication, providing data analytics services to libraries, opening access to public domain serial literature, developing libraries as partners in civic data ecosystems, adapting military orientation for student veterans, creating toolkits for system migrations, using machine learning for web archive analysis, preserving electronic government information, developing roadmaps for 3D and VR services, and creating VR/AR programs for health sciences libraries.
